<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech real farm revenues rise 15 pct yr/yr in Sept.</title>
<headline>Czech real farm revenues rise 15 pct yr/yr in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total revenues from Czech farming enterprises rose 15 percent year-on-year in September, in inflation-adjusted terms, putting revenues for January-September down 0.9 percent, the Czech Statistical Office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The figures refer to the sale of own goods and services in total.</p>
<p>Revenues from agricultural production alone were up 16.2 percent year-on-year in September but down 1.8 percent in the January to September period.</p>
<p>The statistical office added that the number of workers employed in the agricultural sector fell in absolute terms to 147,501 from 148,521 in the previous month but was five percent lower than in September 1995.</p>
<p>The average monthly farm wage was 8,263 crowns, down from 8,579 in August.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
